# KyzerDocs Lite — product environment contract.
#
# This is the file a BUYER copies to .env.local. Keep it minimal: every variable
# here is something a non-technical small-business owner must obtain and paste in.
# Adding a variable to this file adds a step to their setup.
#
# The eval harness has its own, separate contract at evals/.env.example. Those
# variables (KyzerDocs API keys, a Postgres connection string) exist only to measure
# the KyzerDocs baseline during Phase 1 development. They must never appear here —
# a buyer has no KyzerDocs instance and must never be handed its credentials.

# Gemini API key from AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey).
# Used for both embedding generation and chat. This is the only account a buyer
# needs to create in local mode.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Password for the single admin user. Set this to anything; there is no user table.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Encrypts the admin session cookie. If left unset, the session key is derived
# automatically from ADMIN_PASSWORD above, so you never have to invent a second secret — only set
# this if you want the session cookie encrypted independently of your login password.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Where the SQLite database file lives. Defaults to ./data/kyzerdocs.db.
# DATABASE_PATH=./data/kyzerdocs.db

# Where uploaded files are stored. Defaults to ./data/uploads.
# UPLOAD_DIR=./data/uploads

# Optional. Chat model calls route through OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/keys) so the chat
# model can be swapped without a code change. The app works fully on GEMINI_API_KEY alone —
# leave this commented out unless you specifically want to change the chat model.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional. Only relevant if OPENROUTER_API_KEY is set above. Defaults to a current, cheap
# Flash-line model.
# CHAT_MODEL=google/gemini-flash-latest
# JUDGE_MODEL=google/gemini-flash-latest

# Cloud mode (Business tier — Vercel deployment only). Leave both lines below absent/commented
# out for local mode; DATABASE_URL presence alone switches the whole app to Postgres + Blob
# storage. The Vercel one-click deploy sets both of these automatically — a local-mode buyer
# never needs to touch this section.

# Postgres connection string (Neon). Set automatically by the Vercel Deploy Button's Neon
# integration — do not set this by hand in local mode.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Vercel Blob read/write token, for uploaded file storage in cloud mode. Set automatically when
# a Blob store is added to your Vercel project — do not set this by hand in local mode.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
